f:T511,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a Sampradaya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A Sampradaya is a living spiritual lineage — a tradition that carries teachings, rituals, mantras, interpretations, and methods from teacher to student across generations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to choose one Hindu tradition forever?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not at the beginning. Early exploration is natural. Over time, most seekers benefit from depth in one coherent path rather than collecting disconnected practices from many traditions at once."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can someone honor both Shiva and Vishnu?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Many practitioners do, and traditions like Smartism explicitly frame multiple deities as valid manifestations of one ultimate reality. The difference is often one of devotional center, not mutual exclusion."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I know whether inquiry or devotion suits me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Ask what feels most alive: investigating the nature of the self, or cultivating loving relationship with the Divine. Most seekers contain both, but one usually acts as the primary doorway."}}]}7:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground selection:bg-orange-500/30 selection:text-orange-100 flex flex-col","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"slug":"spiritual-traditions-paths","pillar":"pillar-hub"}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$f"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"CollectionPage\",\"name\":\"Spiritual Traditions & Paths\",\"description\":\"A pillar hub for Shaivism, Vaishnavism, Shaktism, Smartism, and the major path choices within Sanatan Dharma.\",\"url\":\"https://open